  "term": "right brain",
  "definition": "In this historical usage, the right brain means the right side of the brain, especially as discussed in relation to speech and writing. The passage describes it as sometimes helping preserve or restore speech when the left side is damaged, and as being linked to reversed or mirror-writing in some cases.",
